<title>CHILE: Chile Enami smelter workers accept pay deal.</title>
<headline>Chile Enami smelter workers accept pay deal.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Empresa Nacional de Mineria's smelting and refining complex at Ventanas have voted to accept a five year pay contract which will come into force on February 1, said Enami.</p>
<p>The 750 workers voted to accept the first of two alternative pay deals offered by management, said a union official.</p>
<p>The plant's workers had ruled out a strike over the collective contract after the union's negotiating commission agreed the basic terms of the pay deal this month.  </p>
<p>Ventanas was the last of Enami's 11 unions to sign a five year collective contract in the current pay round.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
